WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.100
Spoiler warning for Attack on Titan.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:15.120
*crashing and punches*

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.120
Eren! Try a Snickers!

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.020
You're not you when you're hungry. Grab a Snickers.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.620
Hello Internet, welcome to Film Theory.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:53.020
The only show to recognize that the best way to stop a skyscraper-tall Titan isn't building a stronger wall,

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.980
It's lining the outside of the city with LEGOs.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.139
Look at those bare feet, LEGOs are gonna be more effective than a spike pit.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:06.140
Anyway, as you can tell, today I'm taking another look at everyone's favorite action horror anime, Attack on Titan.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.949
Now if you're unfamiliar, check out the last video that we did about it or quite frankly,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.749
just watch the series. If you're new to anime and overwhelmed by which shows you should be aware of,

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:18.020
this is definitely one of them. It's one of those franchises

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.360
that'll just remain a must watch anime for years to come, kinda like Death Note and Full Metal Alchemist.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:29.720
Anyway, to give you the three sentence rundown, for 100 years, all of humanity has been living in fear, locked in cities protected by

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.569
towering stone walls designed to keep out the man-eating giants

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:39.889
known as Titans. One boy, named Eren Jeager, becomes a soldier and years later discovers that he has the ability to turn into a Titan

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.819
at will. With Eren's new power, humanity finally has a fighting chance against their ancient enemy,

00:01:43.819 --> 00:01:45.979
but reclaiming the world will still be a uphill

00:01:45.979 --> 00:01:50.809
battle. Especially when you consider that Eren tends to get kidnapped more often than Princess Peach. Now

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:54.860
it'll come as no surprise that the biggest reason I love watching Attack is that it's packed to

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:59.270
bursting with unsolved mysteries. Mysteries is like what the heck was in Eren's basement?

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:05.149
Why the heck would the Colossal Titan knock down the wall in the first place? And how long will this newly-introduced character last before -

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:05.810
oh, wait, never mind,

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.310
they just died. But there's been one question that's been hanging over the series since the very beginning. One

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:14.160
that is the single biggest driving mystery of the entire plot. What

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:17.959
exactly are the Titans? Where did they come from? Now

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:21.439
I see you running down to the comments to shout, "TITANS ARE PEOPLE!" and yeah,

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.729
I am very well aware that at the core of every Titan there's a human nervous system piloting it.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:28.160
It's like some kind of horrifying zombie fleshman.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:34.279
But that doesn't tell us what they're made out of. What their origin is. Because while the human body can do some amazing things, one

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:38.209
thing I'm pretty sure it can't do is suddenly grow to 20 times its size.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:43.190
At least not on its own. The laws of physics are pret-ty clear about that one.

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.259
You can't just create matter from nothing.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.300
So when Eren (and the other humans) transform into Titans, all of that instant Titan has to come from somewhere.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:56.260
Something has got to be making that happen, and by analyzing the physical characteristics of the Titans, we can figure out exactly

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.780
what it is. Solving the show's single biggest mystery before it's ever revealed.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:06.049
Now the most obviously unusual trait for the Titan is, of course, they're freaky faces.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:09.260
But right after that, the thing that stands out most about them is their size.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:16.520
Excluding Abnormal Titans like the Colossal Titan and the Beast Titan from Season 2, Titans range in height from 4 meters to a whopping

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:22.940
15 meters tall (or about 13 to 50 feet). That is pretty darn enormous.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.630
"How big did you get? 21 feet.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:27.620
65." Stop bragging about yourself Ant-Man. We heard you the first time.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:31.320
Or at least those of you who watched my recent theory about Ant-Man and the Wasp heard it.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.580
And if you did, you'll remember that, due to the square-cube law, increasing a human body's size by that scale

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:43.790
dramatically changes the ratio between its weight and effective strength, making it much harder for the body to move and support itself.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:49.309
That's why at 60 feet tall, Scott Lang's movements have to be so much slower and more careful.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:53.720
His body is supporting much more weight than it's designed to. And since Titans have bone

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:58.999
structures that are very similar to humans, you would expect them to be a lot slower than the humans fighting them

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.640
But that's not actually the case. In the anime,

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:06.919
we frequently see Titans running towards their human prey and picking them up with the precision and agility of a

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.140
regular-sized human. Even at a full

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.530
15 meters tall

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:17.809
Eren's Titan form is capable of breaking into a sprint and using hand-to-hand combat techniques made for a human a tenth of his size. The

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:22.880
reason for this is explained in Episode 15 by Hange Zoe, the show's resident Titan expert.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.980
(and apparently digi-destined, if those goggles are any indication)

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.020
"I'd kicked the severed head of a three meter Titan out of spite,

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.380
It weighed next to nothing, contrary to the appearance of density and great mass

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.570
The severed limbs were the lightest tree-bark."

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.879
Despite gaining a lot of volume when they transform, Titans don't gain an equivalent amount of mass.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:47.140
They're lighter than they should be, which both explains how they can move so quickly and points towards an interesting conclusion.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:52.020
When Titans transform, some matter is being added to their bodies, but what's there is also

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:56.300
expanding, like a balloon or a loaf of bread rising in the oven

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:03.800
That's the only way they could be increasing in size without also increasing proportionally in weight. And as strange as it sounds, the bread

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.460
comparison might not be that far off.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.320
The thing that causes bread to rise is yeast.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:12.740
A single-celled fungus that to put it very simply eats sugar.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:18.020
"Eating sugar?" "No papa." "Telling lies?" "YES. YES."

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:21.940
And then poops out alcohol and carbon dioxide through a process called fermentation.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:28.760
This trait makes yeast invaluable in the production of beer and wine and has made it a vital component in baking for thousands of years

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:34.909
The gases created by yeast create pockets of air inside of bread dough that causes it to rise and gives the final baked good a

00:05:34.909 --> 00:05:40.980
light fluffy texture (or at least that's what I've learned from binging five seasons worth of the Great British baking show).

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:46.000
And yeast is also what's caused the Titan epidemic in the anime. You heard that right.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:51.170
The true villain and Attack on Titan is a bread leavening agent. Bread is Titans! And

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.580
Titans are people! So-. Oh god, we need to stop Sasha before she kills again!

00:05:58.559 --> 00:06:02.419
If you think that theory sounds like a stretch well good because that's how you activate yeast

00:06:02.419 --> 00:06:05.748
But seriously the yeast theory accounts for some oddly specific

00:06:06.119 --> 00:06:12.949
querts of the physiology of Titans. Firstly, Titans are hot. And now I'm not talking about the Female Titan's exposed muscle

00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:14.949
look that leaves almost nothing to the imagination.

00:06:15.209 --> 00:06:16.610
Get your minds out of the gutter!

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:21.889
I mean that the Titan bodies give off an insane amount of heat (and the bigger they are the hotter

00:06:21.889 --> 00:06:24.739
they tend to be). While regular Titans are hot to the touch, the

00:06:24.869 --> 00:06:30.439
Colossal Titan can cook anyone trying to attack him with a burst of hot steam. And the Massive Titan that Rod just

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:36.558
transformed into in the anime is so hot that trees burst into flame just from being near him. Now

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.320
look at yeast. As yeast ferments, it gives off heat. It's an exothermic

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:48.560
reaction. If the fermentation process speeds up or more alcohol is being produced, that temperature rises. Bigger sizes, faster growth, more

00:06:48.689 --> 00:06:50.479
HEAT. With bigger Titans,

00:06:50.479 --> 00:06:56.748
the fermentation would be happening at such great volumes and speeds that the resulting heat would cook the air around them.

00:06:56.809 --> 00:07:02.088
We can see clear evidence of this whenever a Titan is wounded or dies. As their skin breaks down and

00:07:02.339 --> 00:07:05.689
decomposes massive amounts of gas are released all at once,

00:07:05.939 --> 00:07:09.199
sometimes with enough force to blow away the soldiers trying to fight them.

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:13.998
This gas would be the CO2 that's being produced by the yeast and that's keeping the Titan bodies

00:07:14.369 --> 00:07:16.699
inflated. And then there's the way that Titans take in energy.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:20.958
Despite having a hankering for human flesh that rivals my own cravings for Diet Coke,

00:07:21.059 --> 00:07:27.799
Titans don't actually need to eat humans for sustenance. I mean, consider this - they were able to keep moving around outside the walls for a

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:33.949
hundred years, but only a few unlucky Survey Corps members to snack on. Nope. Their fuel isn't humans.

00:07:33.949 --> 00:07:41.359
The only thing that Titans actually need to keep their insanely huge bodies moving is sunlight. In Episode 15, Hange proves this by covering our

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:47.329
two captive Titans, Sunny and Bean, with tarps, causing them to stop moving entirely in just a matter of

00:07:47.459 --> 00:07:53.539
hours. And the Titans discovered inside the walls after Eren and Annie's wrestling match at the end of Season 1 are also shown to be

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.998
completely immobile due to a lack of sunlight.

00:07:56.069 --> 00:07:58.398
You know what else draws energy from sunlight?

00:07:58.589 --> 00:08:04.939
Yeast. When exposed to ultraviolet radiation from the Sun or other sources, yeast becomes more active, growing,

00:08:05.399 --> 00:08:08.719
reproducing, and fermenting at a faster rate than normal. If that

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.289
fermentation is truly the source of the Titans energy, that would explain why

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.979
cutting them off of sunlight causes them to slow down and eventually stop

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:20.299
moving. So ladies and gentlemen, what we have here is a classic case of yeast infection.

00:08:20.849 --> 00:08:26.479
Okay, so maybe not your 'classic' yeast infection. And we're obviously not just talking about normal yeast.

00:08:26.659 --> 00:08:32.809
I mean, FatPat here eats a lot of bread and not once has it inspired a global crisis. Just a waistline crisis.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:36.799
Which merits the question: is yeast just an inspiration for Titan behavior?

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.039
Or is it truly the cause of what we're seeing in the anime?

00:08:40.039 --> 00:08:46.249
Is there any sort of evidence that the Attack on Titan universe would have some sort of special yeast that could produce these sorts of

00:08:46.249 --> 00:08:53.460
effects? Yes. Yes, there is. It's subtle, (certainly subtle enough that most viewers would probably overlook it) but it is absolutely

00:08:53.460 --> 00:09:00.440
there. In the publicly available information bonus sections from the manga (which are then repurposed as commercial break eye caches for the anime)

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:07.429
There's an entire page dedicated to a unique type of yeast produced behind Wall Sina. Reading both anime and manga

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:10.820
descriptions of it, we learned that this special yeast doesn't come as a powder.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.659
It looks like a lump of fermented soybeans the size of a human head.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:19.789
What's more, storing it with wheat, soybeans, or cured meat slows down the decomposition process,

00:09:20.459 --> 00:09:27.679
transforming the food by some means not yet explained by science. This preservation ability provided through the yeast allows for supplies to be

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:33.380
stockpiled for future use by forces fighting to take back the walls. And, while that might not seem suspicious at first

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:38.179
every other one of these pages is either directly relevant to the current

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:45.919
storyline or provides vital world building details, covering topics like characters, battle gear, details about the walls, the history of Titan attacks,

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:50.029
Etc. And only 14 of these sorts of pages are included in the original manga

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:57.560
These aren't throwaway details. Each and every one of these pages is something that the manga's writers felt that you needed to know.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:04.070
So it's strange at the very least to think that we need to know this weird little detail about fantasy-world food preservation,

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:08.209
unless it isn't really about the food preservation at all.

00:10:08.810 --> 00:10:09.110
You know,

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:16.880
there's one other place in the Attack on Titan universe where we see that kind of unnatural preservation ability: in the bodies of the Titans

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.239
themselves. When we find out Ymir's backstory in Episode 35,

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:25.549
we see her turned into a Titan as punishment for leading a cult (and being forced to spend decades out in the wilderness).

00:10:26.010 --> 00:10:30.710
Eventually, she gets completely buried in the dirt before Bertholdt, Annie, and Reiner stumble up on top of her.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:32.809
But when she transforms back into a human,

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.179
she somehow hasn't aged a day.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:41.179
Something within her Titan body preserved her perfectly for all of those years. In general,

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:46.340
there's something preventing the bodies and minds of the human hosts from aging or decaying for years inside

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:54.040
their transformed states. And the only thing we know with that property (which also conveniently would explain the Titans' light weight to gassiness

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:57.960
and their solar-powered physiology) is Wall Sina's miraculous

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:04.790
Giant-sized yeast. So the next time you're baking bread just make sure you eat it before it eats you.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.600
But hey, that's just a theory.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.920
A Film Theory.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.100
AND CUT

